 The method of proof follows roughly the method of proof of <span class="cite">[<span class="postnote">Theorem 1</span>, <a href="/bibliography/Faltings-algebraisation">Faltings-algebraisation</a>]</span> and <span class="cite">[<span class="postnote">Satz 2</span>, <a href="/bibliography/Faltings-uber">Faltings-uber</a>]</span>. The result is almost the same as <span class="cite">[<span class="postnote">Theorem 1.1</span>, <a href="/bibliography/MRaynaud-paper">MRaynaud-paper</a>]</span> (affine complement case) and <span class="cite">[<span class="postnote">Theorem 3.9</span>, <a href="/bibliography/MRaynaud-book">MRaynaud-book</a>]</span> (complement is union of few affines). 